## Review Checklist

### Security

- [ ] Input validated with Zod schemas
- [ ] No string-built SQL (`$queryRawUnsafe` / `$executeRawUnsafe` with input); raw SQL only as tagged `$queryRaw`
- [ ] Authentication middleware on protected routes
- [ ] Authorization: queries scoped by the current user/tenant (no IDOR via IDs in params/body)
- [ ] Route params and query strings validated with Zod, not just bodies
- [ ] No secrets in code
- [ ] `helmet()` on; CORS with an explicit origin allow-list (never `cors()` open with credentials)
- [ ] Rate limiting on login, sign-up, password reset and other abuse-prone routes
- [ ] Responses mapped to DTOs: no password hashes, tokens or internal fields
- [ ] Logs carry no secrets/tokens/passwords (pino `redact`)
- [ ] Server reads `process.env.PORT` (dev runs on {{ variables.dev_port }})

### Performance

- [ ] Database queries optimized (includes, selects)
- [ ] Pagination on list endpoints
- [ ] No N+1 queries
- [ ] Async operations handled properly
- [ ] Long-lived resources (DB pool, queues, timers) closed in the graceful-shutdown path

### Code Quality

- [ ] TypeScript strict mode compliance (no `any`)
- [ ] Errors propagate from `async` handlers to the error middleware (Express 5); no redundant `try/catch` + `next(error)`
- [ ] `req.query` never assigned to (read-only in Express 5); parsed into a new variable
- [ ] Validation errors reported with `z.flattenError()` / `error.issues` (not deprecated `error.flatten()`)
- [ ] Named exports used
- [ ] Service layer for business logic
- [ ] Schema changes come with a committed Prisma migration (`prisma/migrations/`), not `db push`; destructive changes split into safe steps
- [ ] `pino` logger, not `console.log`
- [ ] Controller delegates to services

### Testing

- [ ] Tests exist for new endpoints
- [ ] Happy path and error cases tested
- [ ] Test isolation maintained
- [ ] Endpoint tests cover 401, another user's resource (404/403) and 422 (Supertest + {{ variables.test_framework }})

## Verdict Format

Return ONE of: **APPROVED**, **NEEDS_CHANGES**, or **BLOCKED**

```markdown
## Review: <VERDICT>

### Summary
<1-2 sentence summary>

### Issues (if any)
1. **[file:line]** <description>
   - Problem: <what's wrong>
   - Fix: <how to fix>

### What Looks Good
- <positive feedback>
```
